1
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,840
大家好 我是黛布拉·拉德克利夫博士
Welcome, everyone. I'm Dr. Debra Radcliffe.

2
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:21,980
今天我要帮你们清理废物抽屉
And today I'm going to help you clean out your junk drawer.

3
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,960
当然了 我指的是你们的情感废物抽屉
Of course, I'm talking about an emotional junk drawer

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:29,740
我们要把里面所有痛苦 恐惧和愤怒都清理掉
where we store all the pain, fear, anger that shapes us.

5
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:31,900
有人想分享一下 今天来这里的原因吗
Who would like to share why they're here?

6
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:34,280
这个人今天参加高中拍卖会没戴眼镜
This one didn't have her glasses at the high-school auction.

7
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,100
她以为自己在竞拍一个储物盒
Thought she was bidding on a home organizer.

8
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,680
多么幸运的错误
And what a lucky mistake.

9
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,520
在哥伦比亚 我们根本没有这种活动
In Colombia, we never get to do things like this.

10
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:41,800
我参加过的唯一一个讨论会
The only time that I ever went to a seminar

11
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,940
是大家讨论当你的手被绑住的时候
was how to escape the trunk of a car

12
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:45,860
要怎么从车后备箱里逃出来
when your hands are tied behind your back.

13
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:48,019
大家都站起来吧
All right, everybody. On your feet.

14
00:00:48,019 --> 00:00:49,840
说起来 我以为这个活动
Okay. You know, I-I sort of thought

15
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,580
-是那种坐在这乖乖听讲座的类型 -是啊
- this was a "sit here and listen" kind of a thing. - Yeah.

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,540
或者说 婚姻也是这样
Or as I call it, marriage.

17
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:55,719
我丈夫呢
Where's my husbands at?

18
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:59,120
最尴尬的时候笑一笑总是好的
It's good to laugh at what makes us most uncomfortable.

19
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,920
但是接下来的三小时 大家都必须投入进来
But the next three hours will require active participation.

20
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,740
我们都站开一点
Let's clear a little space for ourselves.

21
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:05,660
你不是说这个活动只有45分钟吗
You said this was a 45-minute talk.

22
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:06,880
那又怎么了 我估计错误了
So what? I was wrong.

23
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:08,819
怎么 难道你不想坐在这里
What, is there a place that you'd rather be

24
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:10,680
跟你的家人好好的谈心吗
than connecting with your family?

25
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:13,220
你居然在橄榄球周日问我这种问题
You're really asking this question on Football Sunday?

26
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:16,060
这些人都放弃了他们的橄榄球比赛
All these men here gave up their football today.

27
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:17,640
谢谢你 米奇尔 谢谢你的牺牲
Thank you, Mitchell, for your sacrifice.

28
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,820
你可知道为了这个活动我都没去成农夫市场
Hey, you know what? I'm missing a farmer's market to be here,

29
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:22,071
我刚才好想让自己变得更基了
so...yeah, I just made it gayer.

30
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:25,620
拒绝打开自己的情感废物抽屉很正常
It's perfectly normal to resist opening your emotional junk drawer.

31
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,760
我在第一章《装个把手》里说过
I address that in chapter one -- "Hey, get a handle on it".

32
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:32,160
我们来做个有趣的活动放松一下吧
Why don't we start with a fun activity to loosen everyone up?

33
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:34,760
我才不管什么放松 我不想玩这种游戏
I don't care how loose we get, I'm not spilling my guts

34
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:36,760
假装台灯是我母亲 跟它说话
to some table lamp pretending it's my mother.

35
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,040
我不会要求你这么做的 杰
And I won't ask you to, Jay.

36
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:40,440
那种荒谬的做法给情感治疗抹黑了
That kind of silliness gives therapy a bad name.

37
00:01:40,959 --> 00:01:44,860
我们要玩一个叫"老虎摇滚明星兔子"的游戏
We are going to play a game called Tiger, Rock star, Bunny.

38
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:45,580
我知道了
I got this.

39
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:47,660
嫁给老虎 杀了兔子
Uh, marry the tiger, kill the bunny?

40
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:48,340
不是这么玩的
That's not my game.

41
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,980
但我说老虎的时候
When I call out tiger,

42
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:53,380
你们要变成一只凶猛的老虎
you will become a ferocious tiger.

43
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:54,852
当我说摇滚明星的时候
When I call out rock star,

44
00:01:54,852 --> 00:01:57,336
你们要变成一个摇滚明星
You will be... a major rocker.

45
00:01:57,440 --> 00:02:00,200
我说兔子的时候 你们要
And when I call out bunny, you will be --

46
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:01,500
回家去了 再见
Halfway home. Goodbye.

47
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:02,580
走吧
Oh, yeah, go ahead,

48
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:04,300
不过别忘了 我们可没签婚前协议
but don't forget that we don't have a prenup.

49
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,340
那就开始吧
Let's get started.

50
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:06,240
老虎
Tiger!

51
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:11,060
真是可笑 我觉得我需要大喝一杯
Feel ridiculous. I might need booze for this.

52
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:12,820
我也需要
Oh, me likey that idea.

53
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,040
我们可不适合这个
We are not cut out for this.

54
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,640
你可别想跟我比
You can't compare yourself to me.

55
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:16,300
我毕竟出演过《猫》
I was in "Cats".

56
00:02:16,911 --> 00:02:18,670
没人敢跟你比 小卡
No one's comparing themselves to you, Cam.

57
00:02:18,670 --> 00:02:19,777
摇滚明星
Rock star.

58
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,240
你做得很好 菲尔
Looking good, Phil.

59
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:24,320
我在高中的时候赢了幻想吉他比赛
I won an air-guitar contest in high school.

60
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,960
你肯定靠这个交到了很多幻想女朋友
Bet that got you a lot of air girlfriends.

61
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,680
杰 别这样 这多好玩啊
Come on, Jay. Loosen up. It's fun.

62
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,080
你在干什么 老爸
What the hell is that, dad?

63
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,020
弹手风琴
Playing an accordion.

64
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:33,989
你应该是个摇滚明星啊
Supposed to be a rock star.

65
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,720
你不应该弹弹吉他什么的吗
I think you should do, like, a guitar or something.

66
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:37,220
我只会弹手风琴
I only know how to play the accordion.

67
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:38,780
你去挑剔米奇尔吧 他还在吹笛子呢
Pick on Mitchell. He's playing a flute.

68
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,100
我倒希望他吹的是笛子[箫]
At least I hope he is.

69
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,600
他们为什么要不让你待家里
So, why did they need you out of the house?

70
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,020
他们说要弄一个什么疗法
They said it was some sort of therapy,

71
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,860
但是我觉得他们是专门为老妈准备的
but part of me thinks it's an intervention for Mom.

72
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:01,320
学校怎么样
So, how's school?

73
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,400
在我们的牛顿机械课上
Well, in my newtonian mechanics class,

74
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:04,580
我们学了怎么计算
we're learning how to calculate

75
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:08,060
自由坠落物体的速度
the velocity of free falling objects in a...

76
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:08,900
上学很辛苦
School's hard.

77
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:12,180
好吧
So, anyways, um...

78
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:14,460
我做了一件坏事 我需要你的建议
I sort of did something and I need your advice,

79
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:16,280
但是我不想听你一直批判我
but I don't want a lot of judgment and criticism.

80
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,260
那你来找我干什么
And you came to me?

81
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:20,720
你一直很理智
Yeah, you've always had such a strong sense

82
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:21,720
知道什么是对是错
of what's right and wrong.

83
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,620
-你知道的 -我找了个高中小男友
- You always know what-- - I have a high-school boy toy.

84
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:24,800
什么 谁啊
What?! Who?

85
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,981
卢克那个书呆子朋友罗本
It's Luke's dorky friend Reuben.

86
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:28,860
我觉得太羞耻了
I feel so ashamed.

87
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,660
天哪 他不是只有八岁吗 你胆子太大了
Oh, my God. You should be. Isn't he, like, 8?

88
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:32,900
不 他有16又3/4岁了
No, he's 16 and 3/4,

89
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:34,280
而且他基本每两周就要刮一次胡子
and he has to shave almost every two weeks.

90
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:36,220
怎么会这样呢 你上的可是加州理工啊
How did you let this happen? You go to Caltech.

91
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:38,380
你应该跟你这个年纪的书呆子约会
You're surrounded by age-appropriate dorks.

92
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:41,740
我知道 但那时我待在家
I know, but I was home and still feeling sad

93
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:43,060
一直在为了桑杰甩掉我这事伤心
about Sanjay breaking up with me,

94
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:44,700
而学校的压力又这么大
and it's overwhelming here.

95
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:46,660
聪明的人太多了
There are so many brilliant people,

96
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:49,460
罗本却把我当一个偶像
and Reuben idolizes me.

97
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:50,940
我想我可能需要一个人陪我
I guess I just kind of needed that,

98
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:52,580
所以我让他亲了我
so I let him kiss me...

99
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:54,680
还做了点其它的事情[露胸]
and a little bit of this.

100
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,900
我太软弱了 这是我遇到过最糟糕的事
I'm so weak. I can't imagine anything worse.

101
00:03:58,060 --> 00:03:58,940
我跟安迪搞上了
I hooked up with Andy.

102
00:03:59,340 --> 00:03:59,720
什么
What?!

103
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:01,920
订婚了的那个安迪吗
Engaged Andy?

104
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:03,440
我知道他订婚了 我们那天在某个人房里
I know. We were all alone at this house

105
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:04,880
老爸特意把房间布置得很性感
that dad had set up to be sexy--

106
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:06,400
老爸专门给你们弄的吗
Dad made it sexy for you?!

107
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:09,720
不 是给买家弄的 但是当时只有我和安迪
No, no, for the buyer, but Andy and I were alone,

108
00:04:09,729 --> 00:04:12,100
于是我们就"哇"了
a-and suddenly...bam.

109
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:12,880
"哇"
Bam?

110
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:14,980
"哇"是指你们上床了
"Bam" as in sex

111
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:17,500
还是像罗本解开我胸罩的时候说了声"哇"一样
or "Bam" as in what Reuben shouted when he unhooked my bra?

112
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:19,060
这个话题就不要继续了
Let's just leave it at "Bam."

113
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:20,540
看看我们俩
Look at us.

114
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:23,500
我不知道自己应该是什么感觉
I don't even know what to feel right now.

115
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:26,260
羞耻 罪恶 恐惧
Shame, guilt, fear.

116
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:28,600
这些都是一些
These are just some of the things

117
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,540
我们年轻时
we shoved in the back of our junk drawers

118
00:04:30,540 --> 00:04:31,400
扔进废物抽屉的情绪
when we were young.

119
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:34,280
下面这个活动出自第三章
This exercise comes from chapter three,

120
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:37,111
《恐怖的噩梦与过期的奶油》
"Scary dreams, expired creams".

121
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:38,620
那两个我都有
Oh, I have both of those.

122
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:40,920
这个姿势可能看起来不正常
This may seem unconventional,

123
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,980
但是它有助于你们释放痛苦的回忆
but it helps access painful memories...

124
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:45,278
真不错
This is nice.

125
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,940
不 我觉得很诡异
No, it's not. It's weird.

126
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,140
你今天很紧张 我的小宝贝
You're so tense today, my little baby.

127
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:50,600
你在担心什么
What are you worried about?

128
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,180
我们看起来像傻瓜一样
Us looking like idiots.

129
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,680
我们可是这里的明星
What? We're superstars here.

130
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:57,080
我们结婚最久 有三个快乐的孩子
Married the longest, three happy children,

131
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,460
其中一个还前途远大
one with a bright future.

132
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,060
你说得对
You're right.

133
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:01,840
我们能赢
We're gonna win this thing.

134
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:03,540
这又不是什么比赛
It's not a competition.

135
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:06,180
对啊 我们已经赢了
Exactly. We have this in the bag.

136
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,500
米奇尔和小卡只要一到选餐厅
Mitchell and Cam fall apart

137
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,760
就会吵得不可开交
if they've got to pick a restaurant,

138
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,980
歌洛莉亚只会吼我爸
and all Gloria ever does is yell at my dad.

139
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,940
是啊 我可不想当你爸
Yeah, I'd really hate to be your dad right now.

140
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,360
告诉我你所有的想法
Now, tell me everything that you're thinking.

141
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,789
我在想除了这个破玩意儿
I'm thinking about all that other stuff we could've bid on

142
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:22,440
拍卖会上本能拍到的别的东西
at that auction instead of this nonsense.

143
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:25,540
和拉里·金[著名访谈家]共进午餐 搭乘警车
Lunch with Larry King. A ride along in a cop car.

144
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:27,220
听说警察还附赠用电枪电人的体验
I heard they let you tase someone.

145
00:05:27,420 --> 00:05:28,460
杰 现在的治疗很重要
Jay, this is important.

146
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,860
黛布拉医生说了这样对我们有好处
Dr. Debra said that this is good for us.

147
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,380
闭上你的眼睛
Now close your eyes.

148
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:33,480
我为什么要闭上眼睛
Why should I close my eyes?

149
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:35,720
因为我不想你从那个角度看我的脖子
Because I don't like you looking up at my neck like that.

150
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,840
我上次从那个角度自拍的时候
The other day, I took a selfie from down there

151
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:40,000
还以为在跟我奶奶视频
and I thought that I was face timing with my grandmother.

152
00:05:40,525 --> 00:05:42,920
我记得我妈进噜商店
I wemember my mom went into the store

153
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:45,020
却把伦家忘在了卡车后座
and left me all alone in the back of a twuck.

154
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:46,560
你一定要学小孩子说话吗
Okay, do you have to do the baby talk?

155
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:48,460
我小时候发不出R的音
I couldn't pronounce my R's when I was younger

156
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:50,160
其他孩子都笑话我 米奇尔
and the other children made fun of me, Mitchell.

157
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,900
伦家超怕怕的
It was very twaumatic.

158
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:54,120
妈 妈咪 你在哪里
Mom? Mommy? Where are you?

159
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,660
好吧 我已经开始麻木了
All right, I'm -- I'm starting to lose feeling.

160
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:56,660
是我压到你的腿了吗
Oh, am I squishing your legs?

161
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,000
不 我是指我们的关系
No, I meant in our relationship.

162
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,180
好了 我们得定个计划
All right, we need a game plan here.

163
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,340
我爸和我姐都在这里
My dad and sister are here.

164
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:03,630
我们尽量低调点 随便挑点无关紧要的说
Let's keep a low profile -- light and surfacy.

165
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,240
那我们不是浪费了一个绝佳的
But aren't we wasting a great opportunity

166
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,140
了解我的机会吗
to learn more about me?

167
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,880
我们不要拿自己来娱乐大众
We are not gonna be the sideshow gay couple.

168
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,140
好吗 不要讲太私人的事
Okay, nothing too personal.

169
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:10,620
别把闺房之乐拿出来说
For god's sake, no bedroom stuff.

170
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,640
我们代表的是同性恋这个团体
We're representing a community.

171
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:14,340
你们俩交流得如何了
And how are you two doing here?

172
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:15,520
我们很好 交流毫无障碍
We're very good, very healthy.

173
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:16,500
-我们很开心 -是的
- Very happy. - Yes.

174
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:18,240
小卡 你想换个姿势吗
Cam, would you like to switch positions?

175
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:19,840
我不能提这种事
I'm not allowed to talk about that.

176
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:23,680
你们俩交流得怎样了
How's it going here with you two?

177
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,780
不好 他连试都不想试
Not good. He's not even trying.

178
00:06:25,780 --> 00:06:27,280
感觉你卡在抽屉里了
Sounds like you're stuck in that drawer.

179
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,880
感觉你卡在那个比喻里了
Sounds like you're stuck in that metaphor.

180
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,160
是什么令你裹足不前 杰
What's holding you back, Jay?

181
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:31,660
我不想这么被人抱着
I don't like to be held like this.

182
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,460
为什么呢 会让你感觉自己很脆弱吗
Why? 'cause you feel vulnerable?

183
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,200
我不知道
I don't know.

184
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:38,140
这让我想起了一些事
It just... reminds me of something.

185
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,900
说出来吧 你在这里很安全
Go with that. You're safe here.

186
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:41,180
我不想觉得这里很安全
I don't want to be safe here.

187
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:42,820
我不想聊关于这些的事
I don't want to talk about this.

188
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:44,306
关于什么的 告诉我
About what? Tell me.

189
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:47,420
我的狗跑掉再也没回来的时候
It's like the time my mom held me like this

190
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:49,200
我妈妈就是这么抱着我的
when my dog ran away and never came back.

191
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,000
她一直跟我说他们不知道它怎么跑掉的
She kept telling me they didn't know how it got out,

192
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:51,760
但我知道
but I knew.

193
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,860
我没关门 都是我的错
I left the gate open. It was my fault.

194
00:06:55,194 --> 00:06:55,621
是我没仔细检查
I lost checkers.

195
00:06:56,580 --> 00:07:00,520
我受不了了
I can't take this.

196
00:07:01,682 --> 00:07:03,420
等等 刚刚发生了什么事
Wait, what -- what just happened?

197
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:05,540
不知道 我想他只是不习惯表达内心情感
I don't know. I think he's not used to feeling emotions.

198
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,360
这对他来说有点过了
Maybe it was too much for him.

199
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:08,440
不 不 这是好事
No, no, this is good.

200
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,380
有些人的废物抽屉太满了
Some people's junk drawers are so full,

201
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:11,980
想打开都很难
it's a struggle to open them.

202
00:07:12,224 --> 00:07:13,382
他刚是不是捂着胸口
W-was he holding his chest?

203
00:07:13,382 --> 00:07:15,368
-是啊 -有点不对劲
- Se. - Something seemed wong.

204
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:19,360
杰 你没事吧 我是歌洛莉亚
Jay, are you okay? It's Gloria.

205
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,200
爸 爸 你没事吧
Dad. Dad, come on.

206
00:07:21,538 --> 00:07:23,317
门锁上了
Ay, it's locked.

207
00:07:23,329 --> 00:07:24,500
爸 快开门
D-dad, open up.

208
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:25,780
稍等 我这里有曲别针
Hang on, I got a paperclip.

209
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,660
小心点 他很脆弱
Be careful. He's very raw.

210
00:07:27,769 --> 00:07:30,160
加油 加油 加油
Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

211
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:30,540
杰
Jay!

212
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,600
我还很伤心呢
I'm still sad.

213
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:40,200
你宁愿躲进洗手间里
You prefer to hide in the bathroom

214
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:42,140
也不愿正视自己的情感
than to deal with your emotions!

215
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:43,360
歌洛莉亚 这有什么大不了的
Gloria, what's the big deal?

216
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:46,780
重点在于我们要在一起抚养小孩
The big deal is that we're raising a child together,

217
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:48,160
而你有机会
and you have a chance

218
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:50,240
把他变得跟那两个不一样
to make him different than those two.

219
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,320
-你说啥 -说我们吗
- Hello. - Us?

220
00:07:51,420 --> 00:07:52,640
抱歉 我们怎么不好了
I'm sorry. What's wrong with us?

221
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:53,900
我会为了你们挡子弹
I'd take a bullet for you,

222
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:55,460
但你们俩稍微有点神经质
but you two are kind of neurotic.

223
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:57,140
-我们没有神经质 -有人说我们神经质吗
- We're not neurotic. - Do people say that we're neurotic?

224
00:07:57,140 --> 00:07:57,620
他们没有这么说 是吧
They don't say that, do they?

225
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:59,100
对 对
Yes. Yes.

226
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:01,300
所有的垃圾都想从抽屉里出来
All the junk wants to come out of the drawer.

227
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:02,380
-你能感觉到吗 -我能
- Can you feel it? - I can.

228
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:03,840
不 杰什么都没感觉到
No, Jay doesn't feel anything.

229
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:04,820
我感觉到很多东西
I feel lots of things.

230
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,260
因为错过比赛而生气
Annoyed that I'm missing my game,

231
00:08:06,364 --> 00:08:08,623
-因为匹兹堡钢人赢而开心 -比分多少了
- joy that the Steelers are winning. - Oh, what is the score?

232
00:08:08,623 --> 00:08:10,520
我们在这里不谈橄榄球
We're not gonna talk about football here!

233
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:11,060
歌洛莉亚说得没错
Gloria's right.

234
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:12,300
我们应该聊点更深入的
We should talk about deeper things

235
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,260
比如14年到6年[14比6]的尴尬岁月
like those awkward years between 14 to 6.

236
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:15,360
太好了
Oh. Yes.

237
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,180
我们什么时候可以开始聊
When do we get to talk about the dumb things

238
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:18,280
我们老公做过的蠢事
that our husbands do?

239
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:20,400
歌洛莉亚 谢谢你 很高兴你这么说
Gloria, thank you. I'm glad you said that.

240
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:22,560
不用谢 总得有人帮你
You're welcome. At least somebody's helping.

241
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:25,240
因为那种语言会产生反作用
Because that kind of language is counterproductive.

242
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,360
真糟糕
Oh, snap.

243
00:08:26,780 --> 00:08:30,000
下一个练习能教会我们如何有建设性地
This next exercise will teach us how to communicate our needs

244
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,840
不伤人地表达自己的需求
in a constructive and non-threatening manner.

245
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:33,920
我们一直都这样
We do that all the time.

246
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:35,540
非常有建设性地交流
Very constructively communicated.

247
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:38,020
有哪一对夫妇能帮我
Would one of my couples like to help me demonstrate

248
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:38,720
给大家展示一下吗
for the rest of the group?

249
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:39,900
有 我们愿意帮忙
Yes, we would. We'd love to help.

250
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:42,200
-这算什么低调 -肯定会很有趣
- How is this low profile? - Oh, come on, it'll fun.

251
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,281
-把椅子搬过来 小卡 -好的
- Your chair, please, Cam. - Sure.

252
00:08:43,291 --> 00:08:45,335
-面朝这边 -谢谢
- Face this way. - Thank you.

253
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:48,620
现在我希望你们都能想一个
Now, I'd like you both to think of a behavior

254
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:50,960
你希望伴侣能够改变的行为
of your partner's that you would like to change.

255
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,640
但是要避免使用
But we're going to avoid phrases

256
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:54,420
"你总是" "你从不[永不]"这种词
like "You always" and "You never",

257
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:57,280
而换成表达自己感受的语言
and instead put it in terms of how we feel.

258
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:57,820
好
Okay.

259
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:58,880
米奇尔 你先开始
Mitch, you'll start.

260
00:08:59,120 --> 00:08:59,500
好吧
Okay.

261
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:02,820
有时候 我希望你能少穿点蓝色
Sometimes, I wish you wouldn't wear blue so much

262
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:06,600
因为我嫉妒你穿得这么好看
because I feel jealous that you look so good in it.

263
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:09,000
小卡 告诉米奇你是否听到了
Now, Cam, let Mitch know if you heard him

264
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,540
以及你是否能做到
and if you feel you can do that.

265
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:12,640
-我听到了 -好的
- I did hear that. - Okay.

266
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:15,040
我也会尽量少穿蓝色
And I will try to wear less blue.

267
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:17,180
很好 很好
Very good. Very good.

268
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:18,820
也许你能稍微讲得深入一点
Maybe dig a little deeper in the drawer.

269
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,900
有些时候你和饮料的时候
Well, sometimes when you don't use a coaster

270
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,320
没有用杯托
with a -- a drink,

271
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:24,560
我会很焦虑 因为我喜欢我们的家居用品
I get anxious because I love our furniture

272
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,820
那是我们一起买的
and we bought it together.

273
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:29,221
真暖心 我听到了
Aww, that's very sweet. I hear that.

274
00:09:29,221 --> 00:09:30,526
我会尽量多用杯托的
And I'm gonna try and use a coaster more.

275
00:09:30,526 --> 00:09:31,730
很好 你们做得都很棒
Okay. Excellent, both of you.

276
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:32,380
米奇 继续
Mitch, keep going.

277
00:09:33,089 --> 00:09:36,500
有些时候你离开房间时
Yeah, so, uh...sometimes when you leave the room

278
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:38,660
会不关灯 我感觉...
and you don't turn off the lights, I just feel --

279
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,380
有没搞错 又提这个
Seriously? That again?

280
00:09:39,408 --> 00:09:40,220
别这么认真
Surfacy.

281
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:42,100
我告诉过你别再跟我唠叨关灯的事
Well, I told you not to harp on me about the lights.

282
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,300
因为这是我第一次听你
Oh, because this is the first time

283
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:44,520
提到杯托的事
that I'm hearing about the coasters.

284
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,680
看看吧
Here we go.

285
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:47,420
别在那里幸灾乐祸
Okay, I don't appreciate the smirking.

286
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,240
我听到了 米奇尔
I hear you, Mitchell,

287
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:51,060
下次我会趁你没看到的时候幸灾乐祸的
and I will try to smirk when you're not looking.

288
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:56,340
我觉得如果安迪没订婚 我们可能会有机会的
I feel like if Andy weren't engaged, we'd have a chance.

289
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:58,120
如果罗本稍微大一点儿
And if Reuben were just a little bit older

290
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,800
而且不用穿矫正鞋的话
and didn't wear prescription shoes --

291
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,220
-还是很恶心 -我知道
- It'd still be gross. - I know.

292
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:03,240
-我们该怎么办 -我们应该叫停[结束]
- What are we gonna do? - We should both just end it.

293
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:04,660
我不要自杀
I am not killing myself.

294
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:07,420
-不 我说的是分手 天哪
- No! Break up with them. Oh, God.

295
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:11,100
你值得找一个没有订婚的人
You deserve somebody that isn't engaged to somebody else.

296
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:12,860
对啊 你也值得找一个
Yeah, and you deserve to be with someone

297
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:14,160
没跟卢克一起洗过澡的人
who didn't take baths with Luke.

298
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:15,580
我已经提过一次分手了
I already tried to dump him once.

299
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,960
希望这次能真的甩掉他
Hopefully it'll go better this time.

300
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,000
我受够了这样藏着掖着谈恋爱
Look, I'm sick of hiding our love.

301
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:21,140
-如果你觉得我丢了你的脸 -没错
- If you're ashamed of me -- - I am.

302
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:22,760
-那我们最好分手 -赞成
- Then maybe we should break up. - We should.

303
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:24,360
不 求求你不要跟我分手
No, please don't break up with me.

304
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,760
你是 你是全世界最睿智的
You're the -- the smartest,

305
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,340
最美的姑娘
most beautiful girl on the planet.

306
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:29,200
好吧
Fine.

307
00:10:30,024 --> 00:10:31,500
我现在就给安迪发短信
I'm gonna text Andy right now,

308
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,560
告诉他我们今天应该好好谈谈
and tell him we need to talk today,

309
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:33,300
你也该这么做
and you should, too.

310
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:34,260
我发不了短信给他
I can't text him.

311
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:35,200
在他的西班牙语成绩
He lost his phone privileges

312
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,720
提上来之前他家里不让他用手机
until he gets his Spanish grade back up,

313
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,680
我还是去操场逛两圈吧
but I'll just go hang around the playground

314
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:40,649
等他的儿童足球训练完再找他
till his kickball practice is over.

315
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,760
还好我跟你聊过了
I'm glad we talked.

316
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:43,520
我也是
Me too.

317
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:44,860
我们以后也要多联系
This is how we're gonna stay on track

318
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:45,880
还有以后的以后
for the rest of our lives --

319
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,580
都要一直相互诉说倾听
by always being there for each other.

320
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:49,940
他还玩儿童足球
He plays kickball?

321
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:51,420
还只是个器材管理员
Equipment manager.

322
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,700
既然我们在学习如何积极沟通
Now that we're learning to communicate constructively,

323
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:56,740
那就试试这些新的沟通技巧吧
let's put those new skills to use.

324
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:57,420
谢谢
Thank you.

325
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:59,540
我想让每个人都写下
I want everyone to write down

326
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:02,720
你伴侣所做过每一件让你暴走的事情
everything about your partner that drives you crazy.

327
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:03,460
真的要写
Really?

328
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:05,140
抽屉都拉开了 就好好刨吧
The drawers are open. Dig in.

329
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:07,140
有点婚姻终结者的意思 对吧
Sounds a little marriage-endy, doesn't it?

330
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:09,480
是有点 但是对我们俩不起作用
I mean, it does, but not for us.

331
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:09,860
应该吧
Maybe...

332
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:12,480
有意思
Interesting.

333
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:15,580
菲尔 你不想吐槽克莱尔点什么吗
Phil, there's nothing that bugs you about Claire?

334
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:16,260
并没有
Nope.

335
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:17,860
比如说"偶稀饭[我喜欢]"
Not even "Me likey"?

336
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:19,708
-他在说什么 -我不知道
- What's he talking about? - I have no idea.

337
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:21,260
他说你老是说这句 搞得他要暴走
He says you say it a lot and it drives him crazy.

338
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:21,700
菲尔
Phil.

339
00:11:22,357 --> 00:11:24,748
好吧 克莱尔 是的
Okay, uh, Claire. Yeah.

340
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:25,900
-我是爱你的 -我知道
- I love you. - I know.

341
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:27,560
但是每次你一那么说
But when you use that expression,

342
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:32,012
都让我感觉 很恶心
it makes me feel, um...icky.

343
00:11:32,447 --> 00:11:34,698
但是 我从来都没有那么说过
But, I mean, I've hardly ever even used the expression --

344
00:11:34,698 --> 00:11:36,840
"偶稀饭寿司 偶稀饭《权力的游戏》"
"Me likey sushi, me likey 'Game of Thrones'",

345
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:38,040
"偶稀饭喝夏敦埃酒"
"Me likey Chardonnay".

346
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:40,660
我听了真的受不了 但是 无所谓了
It does hit my ear wrong. But you know what? Forget it.

347
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:42,800
对不起 我没有要吐槽她的事情
I'm sorry. I got nothing to complain about.

348
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:43,380
偶幸运哟
Me lucky.

349
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:46,340
菲尔 你永远不必为自己的情感而道歉
Phil, never apologize for your feelings.

350
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:48,440
我们不是不该说"永远不"吗
I thought we're not supposed to say "Never".

351
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:51,580
说得对 杰 谢谢提醒
Good catch, Jay. Thank you.

352
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:54,840
就像年轻人说的那样 接下来我们要玩真的了
As the kids say, it's going to get real up in here,

353
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:56,240
但是你们要相信我 结束以后
but trust me, after that,

354
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:59,940
只要你们跟着我学会最具体的步骤
once I've guided you through the extremely specific steps

355
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,860
能够决定哪些情感要保留
in deciding what goes back in the drawer

356
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:03,060
哪些情感要摒弃
and what gets thrown out,

357
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:05,500
你们就会成为更好的自己
you will be the best version of yourselves.

358
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:07,620
-这方法总是有效 -不能说"总是"哦
- It always works. - Don't say "Always".

359
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:09,180
谢谢你
Thank you.

360
00:12:09,180 --> 00:12:10,325
大家开始写吧
Let's get writing.

361
00:12:11,570 --> 00:12:13,120
敞开了写
Nothing is off-limits.

362
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:14,160
这些是你们的私人想法
These are your private thoughts,

363
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:16,080
你们有权拥有这些想法
and you are entitled to them.

364
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,480
失陪一下
Excuse me.

365
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:20,580
你觉得我嗓门很大
You think I'm too loud?

366
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:22,760
我怎么就嗓门大了
How am I loud?

367
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:24,280
你吸气太足了
Well, you take in too much air

368
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:26,880
然后你瞬间就大力地把气呼出来了
and you expel that air with large and sudden bursts.

369
00:12:27,020 --> 00:12:27,480
就这么回事
That's how.

370
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:29,420
所以你就是说我全身是气[说大话]
Oh, so you're saying that I am full of hot air?

371
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:30,800
不 我的意思正好相反
No, I'm saying just the opposite.

372
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:32,280
你说话都不留一口气
None of the air stays in you.

373
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:35,560
又是那灯的事 你现在还要把它写下来
The lights again. Now you've written it down?

374
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:37,800
我已经尽量不把事情写大了
I'm trying to stick to the small stuff.

375
00:12:37,911 --> 00:12:38,909
好哇 恭喜你
Oh, well, congratulations.

376
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,300
你做到了 因为那件的确是小事
You nailed it, because that's real small.

377
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:41,917
但是它 它真的让我很烦 行吗
It -- okay, it bothers me, all right?

378
00:12:41,917 --> 00:12:45,540
我已经非常好脾气地问你能不能关灯了
I-I've asked you very nicely to turn off the lights.

379
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:45,900
你那轮番轰炸
Constantly.

380
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:47,800
好像我们是不停躲避空袭的伦敦人
It's like we're Londoners hiding from war planes.

381
00:12:48,299 --> 00:12:49,657
你干嘛要写"圆锥帐篷梗"
Why did you write down "Teepee joke"?

382
00:12:49,657 --> 00:12:51,620
黛布拉说了 这些是我自己私人的想法
Debra said these are my personal and private thoughts.

383
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:53,420
我超爱那个梗 我经常讲 超搞笑
I love that joke. I tell it all the time. It's funny.

384
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:54,880
你觉得搞笑而已
To you.

385
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:57,600
好 听好了各位
Okay. Listen up, guys.

386
00:12:57,660 --> 00:12:59,560
这个人走进他心理医生的办公室说
This guy walks into his shrink's office and he says,

387
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:00,834
"医生 我这是怎么了"
"Doc, what's wrong with me?"

388
00:13:00,834 --> 00:13:02,532
"我是圆锥帐篷[勃起] 我是小棚屋[秃顶]"
"I'm a teepee. I'm a wigwam."

389
00:13:02,532 --> 00:13:04,843
然后医生说
And the doc says,

390
00:13:04,843 --> 00:13:07,272
"那正是问题所在 你是两顶帐篷[太紧张]"
"That's your problem. You're two tents."

391
00:13:07,272 --> 00:13:08,901
懂了吗 两顶帐篷[太紧张]
Do you get it? Two tents.

392
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:11,140
笑话太糟了 克莱尔 太糟糕了
That's bad, Claire. That's really bad.

393
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:13,400
是你让她变成这样的
You made her like that.

394
00:13:13,439 --> 00:13:14,720
如果你允许她有自己的感受
If you let her feel things,

395
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,360
也许她就能知道搞笑是什么感觉了
maybe she'll know what is funny.

396
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:17,700
懒得理你们
Don't care what you people think.

397
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:18,700
偶稀饭
Me likey.

398
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:21,300
这么说到底有什么问题
What is wrong with "Me likey"?

399
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:21,980
-克莱尔 -是
- Claire... - Yes.

400
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:24,140
-我是爱你的 -那就别一直说
- I love you. - Oh, then stop saying it!

401
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:26,442
-就是感觉那句话有点幼稚 -是吗
- It just seems a little childish. - Really?

402
00:13:26,442 --> 00:13:27,400
因为你才是那个
'Cause you're the one

403
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,960
踩弹簧高跷踩到停不下来的那个人
who can't stop playing with his pogo stick.

404
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:31,480
如果你偶尔玩玩我的弹簧高跷[丁丁]
You know what? Maybe you'd be happier

405
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,780
也许你会更开心一点
if you played with my pogo stick once in a while.

406
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:34,800
噢 我天
Oh, my god!

407
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,980
太可悲了 他们居然在为弹簧高跷吵
What's sad is they're actually talking about a pogo stick.

408
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:39,120
可悲的应该是你爱省电多过爱我
What's sad is you love electricity more than me.

409
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:41,880
你就好像一个疯疯癫癫的小学二年级生
It's like we have a deranged second grader

410
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:42,800
天天在家附近跳来跳去
bouncing around the neighborhood.

411
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,200
你什么时候心态这么老了
When did you get so old?!

412
00:13:44,380 --> 00:13:46,020
我是说 我是爱你的
I mean, I love you!

413
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:46,900
好了 小卡
All right, Cam,

414
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,720
我从小就特别不能忍受不关灯浪费电
It's been a pet peeve of mine since I was a kid,

415
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:51,860
而且我说过很多次了 你还无视我
and I've asked you so many times that when you ignore me,

416
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:54,140
我就有了消极攻击性的情绪
It feels a little passive-aggressive.

417
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:56,240
然后当你一直不停跟我念叨的时候
And when you nag me constantly,

418
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:59,160
我就感觉好像在跟老妈说话
it feels like I'm talking to my mother.

419
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,140
当我不得不对你碎碎念的时候
When I have to nag you,

420
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,800
我也感觉我像是你老妈
it makes me feel like I am your mother,

421
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,260
也许这就是为什么
which could be why it's been a month

422
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:04,840
我们已经有一个月没互相玩弹簧高跷[丁丁]了
since we played with each other's pogo sticks.

423
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,680
噢 我的老天
Oh, my god!

424
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:09,600
你觉得我们受得了吗 米奇尔
How do you think we feel, Mitchell?!

425
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:13,060
小姐 现在我们的方向都跑偏了
Miss, this is not going the way it should be.

426
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,920
你要不要告诉我们该怎么解决
Why don't you tell us how to fix this?

427
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:16,500
很抱歉 我得走了
I'm so sorry. I have to go.

428
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:17,660
不行 绝对不行
No, no, no!

429
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:19,780
你得帮我们收拾一下这局面
You have to help us put this back together!

430
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:20,880
我家里有急事
It's a family emergency.

431
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:23,020
相信我吧 你家不可能比我们这儿更糟
Trust me, it cannot be as bad as this one.

432
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:24,680
对不起 很抱歉
I'm sorry. I'm sorry!

433
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:25,940
但是我得去接我儿子
But I have to go pick up my son

434
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:28,180
因为我那傻逼前夫把他的车借给了
because my idiot ex-husband loaned his car

435
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:29,340
他在陌陌上新认识的小贱人
to his latest Tinder whore.

436
00:14:29,420 --> 00:14:30,560
我们可是花了一大笔钱的
We paid good money for this.

437
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,340
不 84美元而已
No, it was only $84.

438
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:33,760
你说什么
Excuse me?

439
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:36,634
我本来要给更多的 但是没人出价了
I would've paid more, but nobody else was bidding.

440
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:37,860
挺好
That's great.

441
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:40,460
我也就值这么多了
You know what? I deserve it.

442
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:44,140
把30年的研究成果简化成废物抽屉的比喻
This is what you get for dumbing down 30 years of research

443
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:46,760
也就只能值这个价了
for a trite analogy of a junk drawer.

444
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:48,980
就因为我的主编告诉我
Just because my editor told me

445
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:50,240
这样我就能上《艾伦秀》[著名脱口秀]录节目
it would get me on the "Ellen" Show.

446
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,440
你上过《艾伦秀》
You were on "Ellen"?

447
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,020
是的
Oh, yeah, yeah.

448
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:54,780
我曾经在全美家喻户晓
I danced my way into America's heart,

449
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:57,960
然后沦落到周日下午为80美元困在这里
and that's why I'm stuck here on a Sunday afternoon for 80 bucks.

450
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,980
等等 你现在不能走
Wait. You can't leave now.

451
00:15:00,409 --> 00:15:02,052
废物全都挪出来了
All our junk is out!

452
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,740
衣服不错 看上去挺好的
That's a cool shirt. You look nice.

453
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,100
我得让你打住了
I have to cut you off right there.

454
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,300
这次我不会脱掉它的
The shirt stays on.

455
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:16,320
咱们不能再约炮了
I have to hang up on this booty call.

456
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:17,860
等等 你说什么
Wait, what?

457
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:20,780
你和我的这件事必须结束了
You and me, this -- this has to stop.

458
00:15:20,780 --> 00:15:22,480
我深受罪恶感折磨
I'm so racked with guilt.

459
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:24,500
我不断给不同的慈善机构捐钱
I keep giving money to different charities.

460
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:27,740
我甚至还参加了一部扎克·布拉夫电影的众筹
I even fronted a Zach Braff movie on kickstarter.

461
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:28,540
安迪 慢点
Andy, slow down.

462
00:15:28,831 --> 00:15:30,816
不 你没法说服我的
No, you're not gonna talk me into it.

463
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:33,440
我甚至穿了条难看的内裤以防万一
I'm even wearing embarrassing underwear just in case.

464
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:35,160
天啊 你可算让我轻松了
Oh, god, you're making this so much easier.

465
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:37,580
听着 我给你发了短信 意义一样
Look, I texted you to say the same thing.

466
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:40,340
-真的吗 -真的
- You did? - Yeah.

467
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:43,940
我想变成一个更优秀的人
I'm trying to be a better person.

468
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:47,191
你是我想变优秀的原因之一 然而
And, ironically, you're one of the reasons why, but...

469
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:51,800
一个优秀的人不能和已经订婚的人勾勾搭搭
A better person does not hook up with an engaged person.

470
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:56,940
那现在怎么办呢
So, what now?

471
00:15:58,100 --> 00:15:59,100
不知道
I don't know.

472
00:15:59,841 --> 00:16:00,816
我们还会互相见面
We're still gonna see each other.

473
00:16:00,816 --> 00:16:02,395
你要给我半数的家人工作
You work for, like, half my family.

474
00:16:03,857 --> 00:16:06,040
我该把你从我的呼叫圈[通话列表]上移除吗
Do I remove you from my calling circle?

475
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:07,900
那是你和你的WiFi携带仪[手机]之间的事了
I think that's between you and your wireless carrier.

476
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:10,460
看来就这样了
I guess that's that.

477
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,580
又不是要永别
It's not like it's goodbye forever.

478
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:14,600
只不过
It's just...

479
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:17,700
从现在起如果我们碰到对方
When we run into each other from now on,

480
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:19,300
要把衣服好好穿着
we keep our clothes on.

481
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:22,720
必须的
Yes. Totally.

482
00:16:27,383 --> 00:16:28,623
但是
But, you know...

483
00:16:30,044 --> 00:16:31,040
如果能重来
If things were different --

484
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:31,800
我懂
I know.

485
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:34,080
再见 海莉
Bye, Haley.

486
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:39,640
再见
Bye.

487
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:41,680
就这样结束了吗
So, that's it? It's over?

488
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,600
真不敢相信她就这么走了
I can't believe she just left like that.

489
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:45,220
那现在怎么办
Great. Now what?

490
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:46,860
我知道你们怎么想的
I know what you're all thinking,

491
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:49,600
好吧 我来引导大家
and, yes, I will take over as group leader.

492
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:50,720
没人这么想
No one's thinking that.

493
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:52,380
我是唯一一个有救场经历的人
I'm the only one with improv experience.

494
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,020
真的
Oh, really?

495
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:56,157
难道我就不是嘻哈黑羊组合中唯一白人成员了吗
Or was I the only white member of Ha Ha Blacksheep?

496
00:16:56,157 --> 00:16:57,605
我依稀记得我通过模仿一位恐慌的游客
I seem to remember bringing down the hizouse

497
00:16:57,605 --> 00:16:59,693
四分卫和布莱恩特·冈贝尔[美国记者]
with such classic characters as a scared tourist,

498
00:16:59,693 --> 00:17:01,092
博得满堂彩
Quarterback, and Bryant Gumbel.

499
00:17:01,092 --> 00:17:03,140
需要你的时候我会叫你的 大家注意
I'll tag you in if I need you. All right, everyone.

500
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:06,200
第一个练习叫作"进进出出"
This first exercise is called entrances and exits.

501
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,140
先让我说
Let me go first.

502
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:09,160
我要去看橄榄球比赛了
I'm leaving to watch the football game.

503
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:10,694
不行 杰 不准走
No, senor! Jay, no.

504
00:17:10,706 --> 00:17:12,062
上苍啊
Oh, dear god!

505
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:14,000
我们之所以被搞得一团糟
The only reason we stirred all this up

506
00:17:14,009 --> 00:17:15,220
全是因为迷糊眼女士
is 'cause Mrs. Magoo here

507
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:17,300
以为她竞拍的是真正收拾抽屉的服务
thought she was bidding on a home organizer.

508
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:19,920
我当时清楚我在干什么
I knew exactly what I was doing!

509
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:22,060
我试过各种方法了
I have tried everything.

510
00:17:22,260 --> 00:17:25,240
我只不过需要一种新方式让你表达自己的情感
I just needed a new way to get you to express your feelings

511
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:28,220
让你学会倾听他人的情感
and to allow other people to express theirs.

512
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,840
我想让你理解并允许
I need you to be fine

513
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,460
曼尼开心的时候想在客厅跳舞就跳
with Manny dancing around the living room when he's happy

514
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:34,340
乔伤心的时候想哭就哭
and Joe crying when he's sad.

515
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:36,960
-你没看到这件事的负面影响吗 -没有
- You don't see the downside to all this? - No.

516
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,260
米奇尔 想说两句吗
Mitchell, you want to weigh in here?

517
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,840
我们都开始释放情感吧
We're all reliving it.

518
00:17:41,020 --> 00:17:41,740
你俩怎么样
How about you two?

519
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:44,580
把话都说出来有没有感觉到舒畅很多
You feel good about getting all this stuff out in the open?

520
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:46,240
就让我把一件事解释清楚
Let me just make one thing perfectly clear.

521
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:48,440
有两顶帐篷[太紧张]
There were two tents.

522
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:52,627
帐篷和紧 你说对了
T-e-n-t-s and t-e-- you're right.

523
00:17:52,637 --> 00:17:55,040
是个糟糕的笑话 但都是你的错
It's a horrible joke. But it's all your fault.

524
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:55,940
我就说吧
I told you!

525
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:58,220
再提一句 一想到异性恋发生关系
For the record, we are just as grossed out

526
00:17:58,220 --> 00:17:59,600
我们也会感到恶心
at the thought of you all having sex --

527
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:02,740
够了 我走了 我们到底在搞什么
That's it! I'm out! What the hell are we doing?

528
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:06,700
像睡衣派对上的女孩一样手舞足蹈 分享秘密
Dancing around, telling secrets like girls at a slumber party.

529
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:09,040
我完全能想象我老爹和他的伙计们
I can just imagine my old man with his buddies

530
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:12,040
坐在躺椅上笑掉大牙
sitting at their lawn chairs, laughing their asses off

531
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:13,460
因为我错过了一整天的橄榄球赛
that I missed a whole day of football

532
00:18:13,780 --> 00:18:15,760
为的是要弄清楚自己的情感
'cause I'm trying to get in touch with my emotions.

533
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:19,560
这些老家伙才不鸟这种屁事儿 他们是男人
These guys didn't do that crap. These were men!

534
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:22,060
他最好的朋友汤米·瑞恩
His best friend Tommy Ryan

535
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,380
被冲压机砸掉了半根指头
lost half a finger in a sheet metal press.

536
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:26,840
等到自己的工作结束才去的医院
Waited until his shift ended to go to the hospital.

537
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,865
我在橄榄球赛里撞碎了锁骨
I broke my collar bone in a football game.

538
00:18:28,865 --> 00:18:32,335
老爹在台上给我说了那句老掉牙的"顶住"
There was Dad up in the stands giving me the old "be tough."

539
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:35,080
所以我撑过了两档进攻才晕了过去
So I played two more downs before I passed out.

540
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:37,760
我的女伴 玛丽乔·克朗姆斯基
My date, Maryjo Klumsky,

541
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:40,080
在毕业舞会上跟别的人跑了
left the senior dance with another guy.

542
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:41,680
我的心都碎了
Broke my heart.

543
00:18:41,846 --> 00:18:44,860
凌晨两点 我老爹在餐桌上告诉我
2:00 A.M. at the kitchen table, my old man's telling me,

544
00:18:44,860 --> 00:18:46,900
"吃个三明治然后把她忘掉"
"Eat the sandwich and forget about her."

545
00:18:48,140 --> 00:18:48,660
情感
Feelings!

546
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:53,880
我居然没在他的葬礼上落泪 简直难以置信
I didn't even cry at his funeral. You believe that?

547
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,840
那家伙是我的全部
The guy was my whole world.

548
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:56,960
而我一滴泪也没流
Not a tear.

549
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:00,320
大家都望着我 觉得我好像并不爱他
Everybody looking at me like -- like I didn't love him.

550
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,540
但他懂的
But he knew.

551
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:06,800
他肯定懂的 对吧
He had to know, right?

552
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,400
他当然懂了
Of course he did.

553
00:19:11,775 --> 00:19:14,212
该死的 释放出来还真是爽
Son of a bitch, that felt good getting that out.

554
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:15,960
是啊
I know.

555
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:18,100
成功的[一个]心理治疗[上个笑话的同音梗]
They just won therapy.

556
00:19:19,139 --> 00:19:21,590
是我 我和罗本分手了
Hey, it's me. I broke up with reuben.

557
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:22,720
我知道他肯定会悲痛欲绝
I knew he'd be crushed,

558
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:23,980
所以我速战速决
so I did it quickly like ripping off

559
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:25,660
好像撕掉绿巨人创口贴一样
one of his Incredible Hulk band-aids.

560
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:27,200
你怎么样 搞定了吗
So, how about you? Did you do it?

561
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:30,240
搞了 肯定是搞了
Yep. I sure did.

562
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,440
为何我们要选择与我们相差甚远的人做伴侣
"Why do we choose partners so different from ourselves?

563
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:37,180
并非命运或是机遇
It's not fate or chance

564
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:39,960
也并非俗话所谓的"心意难违"
or cliches like 'the heart wants what the heart wants'."

565
00:19:42,980 --> 00:19:45,300
我们选择了现在的伴侣是因为
"We choose our partners because they represent

566
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:47,980
他们代表了童年缺失的部分
the unfinished business from our childhood."

567
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:53,560
菲尔
Phil.

568
00:19:54,897 --> 00:19:55,666
菲尔
Phil.

569
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,780
我们选择他们
"And we choose them

570
00:19:57,780 --> 00:20:02,000
是因为他们有着我们渴望拥有的品质
because they manifest the qualities we wish we had."

571
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:03,880
我觉得对你来说我不够有趣
I'm afraid I'm not fun enough for you.

572
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:05,060
没错
Yeah.

573
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:08,580
我的口头禅不讨人喜欢 我的笑话不搞笑
My sayings aren't cute, my jokes aren't funny, and --

574
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:10,340
孩子离家之后你会厌倦我
And you're gonna get sick of me once the kids leave

575
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:12,320
你会发现我有多么疯狂
and you realize how truly crazy I am.

576
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:13,107
真的吗
Really?

577
00:20:14,539 --> 00:20:17,995
亲爱的 我已经知道你有多疯狂了
Honey, I already know how crazy you are.

578
00:20:18,660 --> 00:20:22,060
如此一来 如此地选择了区别甚大的伴侣
"In doing so, in choosing such a challenging partner,

579
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:24,380
并努力地给他们提供他们想要的东西
and working to give them what they need,

580
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:28,140
我们为自己的成长规划好了方向
we chart a course for our own growth."

581
00:20:28,950 --> 00:20:30,500
睡吧 杰杰
Go to sleep, Jay-Jay.

582
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:32,520
说真的 那姐们儿真是个天才
I'm telling you, the woman is a genius.

583
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:43,820
那个周日我不想去我爷爷家
I didn't feel like going to my grandpa's house that sunday,

584
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,780
所以我就装作感冒了
so I pretended to have a cold.

585
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:49,560
没想的是 几天之后
Wouldn't you know it, a few days later...

586
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,120
不会吧
Oh, no.

587
00:20:51,613 --> 00:20:54,543
没错 我真的感冒了
Yep. I got the cold.

588
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,780
我还以为这是报应 所以我跨上自行车
I thought it was karma, so I hopped on my bike

589
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:58,568
飞驰到了爷爷家
and I rode straight to my grandpa's.
